WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Telemetry forms the foundation of modern security operations.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:08.130
Visibility enables detection, investigation, response, threat hunting, reporting,

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.590
and continuous improvement.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.030
Useful telemetry comes from many sources, including identities, endpoints, applications,

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.482
networks, cloud services, infrastructure, and security tools.

00:00:17.482 --> 00:00:20.964
Collection should be driven by security questions and business priorities.

00:00:20.964 --> 00:00:25.030
Teams need to know which sources exist, who owns them, what activity they record,

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.290
how long they retain data,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.580
and which gaps could prevent an important detection or investigation.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.080
Quality matters as much as volume.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.240
Completeness, accuracy, timeliness, normalization, enrichment, retention,

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.080
and coverage determine whether analysts can rely on the data.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.210
Monitoring source health and testing expected events help keep visibility dependable as

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.135
systems change.

00:00:43.135 --> 00:00:47.200
Organizations that understand and continuously refine their telemetry are better

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.160
positioned to manage cybersecurity risk.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.940
The goal is not to collect everything.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.570
The goal is to maintain the evidence needed for informed defensive decisions when those

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:55.560
decisions matter.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.995
A sustainable telemetry program assigns owners, documents purposes,

00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:02.140
protects sensitive data, monitors cost and source health,

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.730
and reviews coverage when technology or risk changes.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:08.060
Managers, engineers, analysts, responders, privacy teams,

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.760
and system owners all contribute.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.720
Their shared work turns disconnected event streams into dependable operational visibility.
